[7] answered
  Channel binding is implementable — but ONLY against the 's'-suffixed passthrough endpoint.
  On the default form the agent's TLS peer is the gateway, and report_data commits to a key
  the agent never sees. Whatever returns an endpoint to an agent must return the passthrough
  form, and the verifier should refuse an endpoint it cannot channel-bind rather than fall back.

